From cbfab6569faedde58826c915c8476a5934ec5703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hockinglee <hockinglee@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:48:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mproi_spi: Add Mini-Pro-I (MinproI) USB programmer driver

Add a driver for the Mini-Pro-I (MinproI) USB SPI programmer,
USB ID 1fc8:300b ("www.zhifengsoft.com" / "WinUSBComm").

The vendor firmware offers a raw full-duplex SPI transfer command with
flags for asserting and releasing CS#, so a transaction can span several
64-byte USB packets. This allows arbitrary flashrom SPI commands,
including 4-byte addressing. The optional "spispeed" parameter selects
the firmware's SPI clock divider index (0 = fastest, default, to 7).

Unit tests emulate the firmware and an SPI flash to cover init/shutdown,
parameter parsing, probing and a full chip read spanning many packets.

Tested on hardware with a GD25Q16: probe, read, write, erase, verify.

Change-Id: I164c7f2e688308b4f025369433f8cc2b02332448
Signed-off-by: hockinglee <hockinglee@gmail.com>
